# {{ name }}

Translate the operator's words into one `hm intent` verb. `.claude/intent.yaml` holds purpose,
metrics and open questions; each goal is `intent/<ID>.md`, `open` or `closed`.
`hm intent status --json` is read-only and LLM-free: read it first when an id is
unclear. On `state: invalid` show the error (an unmigrated layout names `hm intent migrate`).

**Fact or question** (the project-knowledge boundary):
A claim that bears on an intent's metric or decision is an intent question (`hm intent question`, open → confirmed or wrong); any other domain fact is a `[wiki:fact]`. Record each claim in one place only and link to it from the other.

## The verbs

```
hm intent status --json
hm intent show <ID> --json
hm intent new <ID> --title-file <f> --statement-file <f> --metric <id> [--scope-file <f>] [--out-of-scope-file <f>]
hm intent close <ID> --observed <met|missed|no_data> --note-file <f>
hm intent metric measure <id>|--all [--dry-run]
hm intent metric record <id> --value <n> --evidence-file <f> [--observed-at <ts>]
hm intent question add <id> --claim-file <f> --status <open|confirmed|wrong> [--text-file <f>]
hm intent question observe <id> --relation <confirms|supersedes|contradicts> --text-file <f> [--claim-file <f>]
hm intent question resolve <id> --status <open|confirmed|wrong> --claim-file <f>
```

Prefix each with `uv run --no-project --with {{ harness_maker_src_path }}`. Write every free-text
value with the Write tool to its own path from `mktemp -t hm-intent.XXXXXXXX` (outside the repo)
and pass the path, never inline text. `-file` list flags take one item per line. `--observed-at`
is a timezone-aware ISO-8601 timestamp and defaults to now; `supersedes` needs `--claim-file`.
`resolve` moves open → confirmed|wrong and wrong → confirmed|open; a confirmed claim changes only
through `observe` first.

## Ask only

Ask with {% if is_codex %}`request_user_input` where available (else a numbered list, then wait){% else %}`AskUserQuestion`{% endif %} at three moments, and nowhere else:

- **create a goal**: draft id, title, statement, metric and target from the conversation, then
  ask in one round, at most 3 questions, only for what the conversation did not state, plus the
  confirmation of the draft. Show the rest under "decided for you". If no metric fits, add one
  to `.claude/intent.yaml` `metrics` in the confirmed draft and run `status` to validate it, then
  run `new`. Never invent a baseline: an unmeasured metric reads `gap: unevaluable`.
- **change a target**: confirm the new value once, edit `metrics[].target`, run `status`, then
  `metric measure <id>` when the metric has `measure`; otherwise say the gap is unevaluable until
  the next record.
- **close a goal**: ask met / missed / no_data / keep open, and run `close` only on a close answer.

Every other write (`metric measure`, `metric record`, `question add|observe|resolve`) runs
without asking and prints one line: `intent: <verb> <id> — <what>`. On an answer other than yes,
or no answer, write nothing and do not retry.

## Where things stand

Read `status --json` and report open goals with their metric's `last`, `target` and `gap`, then
metrics whose `reason` is `never_measured` or `stale_definition` (with `how_measured`), then open
questions. For a metric with `measure: true`, `metric measure --all --dry-run` shows what a
record would write. Suggest a goal only when the operator asks what to do next.

Records change only through these verbs and a closed goal never changes; whether the work
serves a goal is the operator's call and the `/hm:execute` review's.
